Jeff Kovach writes:
   I've got a small problem.  I am running the msdos version of 3.1 compiled
   with the microsoft compiler.  I can only run it on lunch hours and breaks
   so I use the save feature alot.  Well, imagine my surprise when I tried
   to load a saved game in 3.1 and it told me "Save game out of date."
   There was no bogus file editing involved.  If I do a save game, and then
   start again I can't load the gave I just saved.  Is there something I don't
   know or am missing, or is this a bug.  I did a quick scan of the doc files
   and didn't find an answer but to be honest, I just jumped right into the
   game without paying much attention to the directions.

Nethack uses your machine clock to insure that it is not loading an
out of date save file.  Your clock is not set correctly and thus
Nethack thinks your save file is too old.  I suggest you set
your clock, not only will this fix your save file problem, you
will also gain access to nifty features based on the time of
day, phase of the moon, and date.

